export const KNOWLEDGE = "# OmniFit Performance: public fact sheet\n\n## Who OmniFit is\n\n- OmniFit Performance is the diagnostic-led personal training practice of Nemezio LopezPerez (Coach Nemezio), based at Teqneeq Functional Health Center, 10772 Thornmint Rd, 4S Ranch, San Diego, CA 92127.\n- Private 1:1 coaching in three formats: in-studio at Teqneeq (a members-only functional health facility; OmniFit is a trainer operating at Teqneeq, not a studio of its own), in-home across North County San Diego, and live virtual coaching anywhere in the United States.\n- Built for professionals 30+.\n- Contact: nemezio@omnifittraining.com · (619) 259-0630. The fastest way to start is to book a consultation at https://calendly.com/nemezio-omnifittraining/45min.\n\n## Who it is for\n\n- Busy professionals 30+ managing demanding schedules: executives and founders, desk-bound and remote professionals, active adults 50+, people returning after a long break or after physical therapy, people burned by bootcamps or big gyms, and couples.\n- People who want joint-friendly strength, better posture, sustainable fat loss and structured accountability.\n- People with joint issues or an injury history who need corrective-first training.\n- Travelers who need a program that works anywhere.\n- Someone who just wants to train is welcome: \"Even if you just want to train, we can start there.\" Train Only is a setting, not a lesser program.\n\n## Who it is not for\n\n- People looking for drop-in classes or group workouts. OmniFit is private 1:1 coaching only.\n- People who want the cheapest option available.\n- People looking for a 6-week quick fix or crash program.\n- People who prefer to train without coaching feedback or accountability, or who are not willing to follow a structured plan between sessions.\n- In-home clients outside the in-home service area. For them, the virtual Executive Reset is the option.\n\n## How it works\n\n1. Consultation. A 45-minute consultation by video or phone, booked with a $30 deposit, refunded the same day you attend your consultation. It is a conversation, not an assessment: no movement testing and no measurements.\n2. Performance Assessment, if OmniFit is a fit. In person at Teqneeq or in your home: $150. It covers the 9-point movement screen, Bodystat QuadScan 4000 body composition, blood pressure, SpO2, grip strength, posture photos and circumference measurements, and sets the baselines for the 12-metric progress framework. The Virtual Performance Assessment for remote and Executive Reset clients is $75: self-measured with live video guidance, posture photos in the app, no Bodystat scan. Either assessment is credited toward your first purchase: a Foundation or Program cycle, an Executive Reset cycle, or a 5-session pack. Programs and session packs start with a Performance Assessment; for a single session it is recommended, not required. A client returning after a lapse of 60 days or more books a new assessment.\n3. Programming. New clients usually start on The Foundation. Experienced clients may start directly on The Program at any tier. Remote clients use the Executive Reset. Single sessions and 5-packs are available without a program. Program graduates can move to the Tune-Up.\n\nStart dates depend on current availability and are confirmed on the consultation. Appointments are confirmed only when payment is received; no slot is held without payment.\n\n## Pricing: the October 2026 card\n\nAll recurring billing is every 4 weeks. No OmniFit product bills by the calendar month. No activation fees, and no processing fees are added to stated prices. Rates current as of October 2026.\n\nTiers are session frequency: Momentum is 1 session a week (4 per 4-week cycle), Performance is 2 a week (8 per cycle), Peak is 3 a week (12 per cycle). Sessions are 60 minutes in studio and in-home, and 30 minutes on the Executive Reset.\n\n### The Foundation (new clients only)\n\nThree consecutive 4-week cycles (12 weeks), paid in one payment at enrollment. Each price is per 4-week cycle; the total is what is due at signup.\n\n- Studio Momentum: $560 per 4-week cycle, $1,680 due at signup.\n- Studio Performance: $1,100 per 4-week cycle, $3,300 due at signup.\n- In-home Momentum: $800 per 4-week cycle, $2,400 due at signup.\n- Studio couples Momentum: $850 per 4-week cycle, $2,550 due at signup (priced per couple).\n- In-home couples Momentum: $1,250 per 4-week cycle, $3,750 due at signup (priced per couple).\n- Not offered on The Foundation: Peak (studio or in-home), in-home Performance, and couples Performance. Those start on The Program.\n- The Foundation is a one-time entry, never a step back. A new client who starts directly on The Program can no longer choose The Foundation.\n- Policy: The Foundation is non-refundable and, apart from your statutory cancellation rights, the 30-Day Fit Guarantee is the only early exit. Two pause weeks are available across the course with notice, extending the end date. Sessions OmniFit cancels are credited.\n- How it ends: after the third cycle you choose whether to continue on The Program at your tier's published rate. Nothing is charged unless you confirm.\n\n### The Program (ongoing, billed every 4 weeks)\n\nContinuation after The Foundation, or direct entry for clients with prior training experience. Charged at the start of each 4-week cycle.\n\n- Studio Momentum: $640 per 4-week cycle.\n- Studio Performance: $1,250 per 4-week cycle.\n- Studio Peak: $1,800 per 4-week cycle.\n- In-home Momentum: $900 per 4-week cycle.\n- In-home Performance: $1,800 per 4-week cycle.\n- In-home Peak: from $2,600 per 4-week cycle, priced by travel and scope and arranged individually.\n- Studio couples Momentum: $1,000 per 4-week cycle (per couple).\n- Studio couples Performance: $2,000 per 4-week cycle (per couple).\n- In-home couples Momentum: $1,450 per 4-week cycle (per couple).\n- In-home couples Performance: $2,900 per 4-week cycle (per couple).\n- Couples Peak: by arrangement.\n- Program terms: 6 pause weeks per 12 months with 2 weeks' notice, credited against the next cycle; 30 days' notice to cancel, with remaining credit applied to the final cycle; reschedule with 24 hours' notice within the same cycle; sessions OmniFit cancels are credited.\n\n### Couples\n\nCouples prices are per couple, not per person. One session credit covers both partners. Studio couples need a Teqneeq membership for both partners. In-home couples need no membership; OmniFit brings the equipment.\n\n### Studio and the Teqneeq membership\n\nEvery studio program, on The Foundation or The Program, requires a Teqneeq membership at $119/mo, billed by Teqneeq. It is Teqneeq's own charge, not an OmniFit charge, and it includes facility access on non-training days. In-home and virtual clients need no membership. Studio non-member session prices include the Teqneeq day pass.\n\n### Sessions without a program\n\nThese are sessions, not a coaching program: no programming between visits and no cycle billing. 60 minutes each.\n\n- Single session: $205 for Teqneeq members, $235 studio non-member (day pass included), $275 in-home. Expires 30 days from purchase.\n- 5-pack: $180 per session for members, $210 per session studio non-member, $250 per session in-home. Expires 8 weeks from purchase.\n- Extra session for clients on a program: $160 studio, $215 in-home.\n- Guest add-on (a guest joins your session): $90 per session.\n- There are no 10- or 20-session packs.\n\n### The Executive Reset (virtual)\n\nLive 30-minute virtual coaching for executives and professionals anywhere in the United States, from home, an office or a hotel room. Billed every 4 weeks, cancel with 30 days' notice, up to six pause weeks per 12 months with two weeks' notice. Starts after the consultation and the Virtual Performance Assessment.\n\n- Bronze: $200 per 4-week cycle. Asynchronous programming only, no live sessions.\n- Gold: $500 per 4-week cycle. 4 live sessions per cycle (one a week).\n- Platinum: $750 per 4-week cycle. 8 live sessions per cycle (two a week).\n- Black: $1,100 per 4-week cycle. 12 live sessions per cycle (three a week).\n\n### The Tune-Up (program graduates only)\n\nOne session per 4-week cycle: a reassessment on the Bodystat QuadScan 4000 and an hour of training, with programming through the OmniFit app between visits. Billed every 4 weeks, cancel with 30 days' notice.\n\n- $295 per 4-week cycle for Teqneeq members.\n- $325 per 4-week cycle for non-members (day pass included).\n- $375 per 4-week cycle in-home.\n\n## In-home service area and travel fees\n\n- In-home training covers North County San Diego. Equipment is provided; no home gym is required.\n- No travel fee in Carmel Valley, Santaluz, Fairbanks Ranch, Rancho Bernardo, 4S Ranch or Poway; it's inside our in-home service area.\n- Elsewhere in the in-home service area, including La Jolla, Del Mar, Rancho Santa Fe, Solana Beach, Encinitas and Carlsbad, a travel fee applies, confirmed before you book. The travel fee amount is not published.\n- For a neighborhood not listed, availability and any travel fee are confirmed before you book.\n- Outside the in-home area, the virtual Executive Reset is available anywhere in the United States.\n\n## Policies (standards that protect your slot and your results)\n\n- Consultation deposit: $30 deposit, refunded the same day you attend your consultation.\n- Rescheduling: 24 hours' notice is required to cancel or reschedule. Sessions canceled with less than 24 hours' notice are forfeited. Rescheduled program sessions must be completed within the same 4-week cycle. Sessions OmniFit cancels are always credited back.\n- Pause weeks: two across The Foundation, with notice, extending the end date. Up to six per 12 months on The Program and the Executive Reset, with two weeks' notice, credited against the next cycle.\n- Cancellation: The Program, the Executive Reset and the Tune-Up end with 30 days' notice; remaining credit applies to the final cycle.\n- 30-Day Fit Guarantee (exact wording): \"If OmniFit isn't the right fit within your first 30 days on The Foundation, The Program or the Executive Reset, tell us in writing and we'll refund the unused portion of your enrollment.\" It is a fit and satisfaction policy. It is not a guarantee of any physical outcome or result.\n- Early exit: apart from your statutory cancellation rights, the 30-Day Fit Guarantee is the only early exit from The Foundation.\n- Changing plans: on The Program you can move up or down a tier between cycles, with notice before the next cycle starts. During The Foundation you can step up, not down; the first 12 weeks are built as a block. If the new tier is only offered on The Program, The Foundation ends at the next cycle boundary and every unused session is credited toward the first Program cycle. There is no move from The Program into The Foundation.\n- Payment: Klarna and Affirm are available to pay over time.\n- HSA / FSA: OmniFit doesn't bill insurance. HSA or FSA funds can be used only with a Letter of Medical Necessity from a licensed provider, available through Truemed. OmniFit provides itemized receipts.\n\n## The Accountability Dial\n\nIncluded at every tier of The Foundation and The Program, and every Executive Reset tier with live sessions, at no price difference. Chosen at the Performance Assessment and changeable at any 4-week cycle boundary, including during The Foundation.\n\n- Full Accountability (the default for the first cycles): daily logging of nutrition, steps and sleep; a coach reply within 1 business day; behavior-change coaching.\n- Coached: a weekly written check-in with a coach reply; 1 to 3 habit targets; a measurement review every 4 weeks.\n- Train Only: sessions plus the app program; a one-tap weekly check-in; nutrition on request.\n- Executive Reset Bronze offers Coached or Train Only.\n- The usual path: Full Accountability, then Coached, then Train Only, then the Tune-Up (graduation, not a fourth setting).\n- \"Tracking is a diagnostic tool, not a life sentence. We measure closely at the start so we can coach less over time. The goal is a client who no longer needs us every week.\"\n- At every setting: payment confirms booking, 24-hour reschedule notice, corrective work in every warm-up, and reassessment at least every 12 weeks.\n\n## What every program includes\n\n- Custom programming built from your Performance Assessment and rebuilt every 4-week cycle.\n- Reassessments on the Bodystat QuadScan 4000 for in-person clients.\n- Nutrition guidance and a macro framework. Nutrition is included in every program; there are no nutrition add-ons.\n- Full access to the OmniFit app for your program, logs and check-ins.\n- Corrective exercise and movement screening.\n- Direct coach access by text or email, matched to your Accountability Dial setting.\n- The Travel Protocol: for studio and in-home clients who travel for work, travel-adapted programming in the app for hotel gyms and rooms, check-ins that continue at your Accountability Dial setting, and pause weeks when a trip can't hold training. During a travel week a scheduled session can be taken live by video instead, at no extra cost. Fully remote clients use the Executive Reset.\n\n## The OmniFit Method\n\nThe OmniFit Method rests on three pillars, carried through four phases: Assess, Correct, Build, Sustain.\n\n- Measured Progress: every program begins with a Performance Assessment, and progress is judged against your own baseline on a fixed cadence, not against an average.\n- Joint-First Strength: corrective work in every warm-up, joint-friendly loading under a 3/10 pain ceiling, and desk-posture work programmed directly.\n- Accountability That Travels: the Accountability Dial, studio, in-home and virtual on one app, pause weeks, and the Executive Reset.\n- Sessions are for form, load and corrective work. The app carries your individual program between sessions, your logs and your check-ins, written for you rather than a template.\n\n## How OmniFit differs from a gym or a class\n\n- A gym gives access and you write your own program; a group class runs one pace for the room. OmniFit writes your program from your Performance Assessment and rebuilds it every 4-week cycle.\n- Measurement: Bodystat QuadScan 4000, nine movement benchmarks, posture photos and strength, against your own baseline.\n- Joints and old injuries are programmed for: corrective work in every warm-up and loading chosen for what your joints tolerate.\n- Between sessions, your program, logs and check-ins live in one app at the accountability setting you chose.\n- When life changes: pause weeks, a Dial you can turn down, tiers you can change between cycles, and the 30-Day Fit Guarantee.\n\n## Injuries, pain and health\n\n- OmniFit trains; it does not diagnose, treat or assess any medical condition, and it is not a medical provider. \"Physical therapy treats; OmniFit trains. We pick up where care ends, coordinate with your clinician when you allow it, and never diagnose or treat.\"\n- OmniFit works alongside external physical therapists and chiropractors, such as Stoke Physical Therapy, and may ask for clearance from your clinician before training.\n- Movement is screened at the Performance Assessment, never on the consultation.\n- Information on the site and in coaching is educational, not medical advice. Consult your physician before beginning any exercise or nutrition program.\n\n## Credentials\n\n- Nemezio LopezPerez, NASM Elite Trainer. Coaching since 2016.\n- NASM: Certified Personal Trainer (CPT), Corrective Exercise Specialist (CES), Performance Enhancement Specialist (PES), Behavior Change Specialist (BCS), Certified Nutrition Coach (CNC).\n- ACE Corrective Exercise Specialist.\n- Precision Nutrition: Level 1, Level 2 Certified Master Coach, Sleep, Stress and Recovery, Nutrition for Metabolic Health.\n- Eden: GLP-1 Fitness, Peptide Fundamentals, GLP-1 Nutrition.\n\n## Reviews and track record\n\n- 4.98 average across 190+ reviews. The reviews are on Google, Yelp, Thumbtack and Bark.\n- About half of clients train with OmniFit for 6 months or longer (see the Outcomes page).\n\n## Useful pages\n\n- Rates: /training-rates-san-diego\n- How it works: /how-it-works-pricing\n- Fit Check: /fit-check\n- The Executive Reset: /the-30-minute-executive-reset\n- In-home training: /in-home-personal-trainer-san-diego\n- Couples: /couples-personal-training-san-diego\n- Corrective exercise and post-rehab: /corrective-exercise-post-rehab\n- HSA / FSA: /hsa-fsa-personal-training\n- FAQs: /faqs\n- Terms: /terms-and-conditions\n";
